lling the race Safe R. Old Democratic-sponsored polls showed Baumgartner up about six, and markets give Conroy only a modest chance, so the forecast stays near the quantitative baseline at roughly R+8.", "watch": "A late surge on affordability and Medicaid themes in the Spokane media market, or fresh public polling tightening the race, would be the main signal to move this toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Michael Baumgartner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Eastern Washington's 5th District has not elected a Democrat in three decades, and first-term Republican Michael Baumgartner is favored to hold the seat against Carmela Conroy in their rematch. The district leans Republican by about five points, and Baumgartner has outraised Conroy roughly three to one, with more than $800,000 banked. Most expert raters place the race in the Safe Republican column, though a few call it Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Conroy about a one-in-nine chance. The two have clashed in debates over affordability, trade, Medicaid and data centers, giving Democrats a hope of narrowing the race in a favorable environment. Still, with no recent independent polling and the incumbent's structural advantages, the race remains on the Republican side of the ledger, likely decided by a mid-to-high single-digit margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0968, "margin": -8.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0951, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0945, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1116, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1005, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1258